{"version": 2, "width": 120, "height": 33, "timestamp": 1793452192, "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "rec_04_damping (cut)"}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2J\u001b[H     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1679 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1680 +\u001b[38;5;231m*New text*: full replacement in `reconcile/SPEC_AMENDMENT_4.3.md`. The substance \u2014                   \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1681 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1682 +\u001b[38;5;231m1. **An upper limit may only be reported after an attempt that failed.** `zeta_attempted` must be    \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1683 +\u001b[38;5;231m   `true` on every row.                                                                              \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1684 +\u001b[38;5;231m2. Three named routes: ring-down, half-power bandwidth, and **the pole of the node's own             \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1685 +\u001b[38;5;231m   rational-fraction fit**, which it was already computing and discarding.\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1686 +\u001b[38;5;231m3. **Window adequacy**: the fit window must span \u22653\u03c4 for the smallest \u03b6 being resolved, and the node\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1687 +\u001b[38;5;231m   must state that ratio. The verifier's existing window is 0.2\u20135.5 s, barely 1\u03c4.\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1688 +\u001b[38;5;231m4. **The limit is void where it contradicts itself**: if any route returns a \u03b6 whose implied         \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1689 +\u001b[38;5;231m   `\u0394f = 2\u03b6f0` exceeds the 0.1 Hz grid, the \"unresolved\" premise is false and the limit does not\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1690 +\u001b[38;5;231m   apply.                                                                                            \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1691 +\u001b[38;5;231m5. Five new audit columns, including `implied_delta_f_hz` so the check above is visible.\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1692 +\u001b[38;5;231m6. Failure is an acceptable outcome: `zeta_method = none` and **`zeta` left empty**, never the grid  \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1693 +\u001b[38;5;231m   formula.                                                                                          \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1694 +\u001b[38;5;231m7. Vivek's scope clause, binding on success or failure.\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1695 +\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1696 +\u001b[38;5;231m*Reason*: E032. The old wording was a specification failure, not a node failure \u2014 the verifier did\r\n\u001b[39m\u001b[49m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1697 +\u001b[38;5;231mexactly what it was told, on all 11 rows.                                                            \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;246m\u2026 55 more lines \u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0Allowed by auto mode\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[39m Now the recording and dispatch:\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[39m Running \u001b[1m1\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[49m shell command\u2026\r\n\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf  $ ./tools/rec.sh start rec_04_damping\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;174m\u273b\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mVibing\u2026 \u001b[38;5;246m(2m 33s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m10.3k tokens)\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[38;5;244m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\